# Kinetic Video Editor — Windsurf AI Rules

## Project Overview
Kinetic is a free, open-source, browser-based video editor built with React 18,
Vite 5, FFmpeg.wasm (@ffmpeg/ffmpeg v0.12), WaveSurfer.js v7, and Tauri v2.
All video processing runs in the browser via WebAssembly — no server, no uploads.

## Exact File Structure (never deviate from this)
```
kinetic-open-source-video-editor/
├── index.html
├── package.json
├── vite.config.js
├── src-tauri/          ← Tauri Rust backend (do not touch unless asked)
├── public/
│   ├── _headers        ← COEP/COOP headers required for SharedArrayBuffer
│   └── assets/
│       ├── kinetic-logo.png
│       └── kinetic-poster-logo.png
└── src/
    ├── main.jsx        ← React entry, never modify unless asked
    ├── App.jsx         ← Header, dark mode toggle, mounts VideoEditor
    ├── styles.css      ← All global styles and CSS variables
    ├── hooks/
    │   └── useFFmpeg.js
    └── components/
        ├── VideoEditor.jsx   ← Main editor shell
        └── Timeline.jsx      ← Horizontal timeline strip
```

## Critical Rules — Always Follow

### FFmpeg
- Always use `@ffmpeg/ffmpeg` v0.12 API: `FFmpeg` class, `ffmpeg.exec()`, `ffmpeg.writeFile()`, `ffmpeg.readFile()`
- NEVER use the old v0.11 API: `createFFmpeg()`, `ffmpeg.run()`, `ffmpeg.FS()`
- Always import `fetchFile` and `toBlobURL` from `@ffmpeg/util`, not from `@ffmpeg/ffmpeg`
- FFmpeg instance lives in `src/hooks/useFFmpeg.js` as a module-level singleton — never instantiate it inside a component
- The `vite.config.js` must always have `optimizeDeps: { exclude: ['@ffmpeg/ffmpeg', '@ffmpeg/util'] }`
- Both dev server and preview server must have COEP and COOP headers set

### React Patterns
- Never use `JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(...))` to copy state that contains File objects — use spread: `{ ...clip, key: value }`
- Always read real video duration via `video.onloadedmetadata` when adding clips, never hardcode a max
- Selected clip index state lives in `VideoEditor.jsx` as `selectedClip`
- All FFmpeg logic stays inside `useFFmpeg.js` — VideoEditor only calls `load()`, `ffmpeg.writeFile()`, `ffmpeg.exec()`, `ffmpeg.readFile()`

### Styling
- All colors use CSS variables defined in `:root` in `styles.css` — never hardcode hex values in JSX
- Dark mode is toggled by adding/removing the `dark` class on `document.body`
- CSS variables: `--accent` (teal), `--accent-2` (blue), `--accent-grad`, `--surface`, `--surface-2`, `--bg`, `--text`, `--muted`, `--border`, `--danger`
- New components get their styles added to `styles.css`, not inline or in separate CSS files
- Use `button.danger` class for destructive actions (red), `button.secondary` for ghost buttons

### Imports
- VideoEditor imports Timeline as `import Timeline from './Timeline.jsx'`
- VideoEditor imports useFFmpeg as `import { useFFmpeg } from '../hooks/useFFmpeg.js'`
- App imports VideoEditor as `import VideoEditor from './components/VideoEditor.jsx'`
- Always include `.jsx` or `.js` extensions in imports

### Code Style
- Functional components only, no class components
- Custom hooks named `useX` and live in `src/hooks/`
- Helper functions like `fmt(seconds)` defined at module level, not inside components
- Prefer `async/await` over `.then()` chains
- Always wrap FFmpeg operations in try/catch and call `setMessage()` on error

