## What NOT to Do
- Never install or use `@ffmpeg/core` as a local npm package — load it from the unpkg CDN via `toBlobURL`
- Never add a backend server — this is a purely client-side app
- Never use `localStorage` or `sessionStorage` — use React state
- Never create separate CSS files per component — all styles go in `styles.css`
- Never use class components or `React.Component`
- Never call `ffmpeg.load()` more than once — the `useFFmpeg` hook guards this with `loadingRef`
- Never store File objects in JSON — always keep them as references in React state
- Never hardcode video duration as 30 — always read from `video.onloadedmetadata`

## When Adding a New Feature
1. Add styles to `src/styles.css` first, using existing CSS variables
2. If logic is reusable, create a hook in `src/hooks/`
3. If UI is a distinct panel, create a component in `src/components/`
4. Wire it into `VideoEditor.jsx` last
5. Test that Export MP4 still works after every change
